# ─── Audit / legal / sensitive documentation — never commit ───────
# These are internal working documents (security audits we ran against
# our own build, defect checklists for the corporate parent site,
# legal-consultation notes, draft notice letters, post-cutover write-
# ups). They contain data we don't want public — defects we found,
# legal posture, and our internal vulnerability counts. The corporate
# handoff PROPOSAL is intentionally excluded from the gitignore so it
# stays in the repo.
docs/security/external-domain-audit-*
docs/security/post-cutover-report-*
docs/security/wavemaxlaundry-site-audit-*
docs/security/wavemax-promo-prelaunch-audit-*
docs/security/parent-site-fix-checklist.*
docs/security/parent-site-footer-defects-checklist.*
docs/security/parent-site-user-testing-checklist.*
docs/security/draft-23-20-notice-letter.*
docs/security/lawyer-consultation-*
docs/security/lawyer-intake-form-*
docs/security/exhibit-*
docs/security/NEW-SINCE-LAWYER-*
docs/security/forensic-evidence/
docs/security/mhr-iframe-embed-patch/
# 2026-06-02: belt-and-suspenders. The specific patterns above missed nine
# files that ended up tracked/public (parent-site-audit-*, seo-comparison-*,
# prod-lockdown-*, SECURITY_REMEDIATION_*, ENCRYPTION_KEY_MIGRATION,
# IMMEDIATE_SECURITY_ACTIONS, csurf-migration-plan). The entire docs/security/
# tree is internal legal/audit working product — blanket-ignore it so no
# sensitive document can slip through a missing pattern again. The intentionally
# public corporate-handoff proposal lives outside docs/security/.
docs/security/
docs/corporate-handoff/
.playwright-mcp/
about-hero-*.png
public/design-explorer/render/

# Claude Code runtime lock files
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Playwright MCP server screenshot outputs that occasionally land in repo root
mhr-payment-*.png
*.playwright-mcp-screenshot.png
.playwright-mcp/

# Stray render/diagram scratch PNGs that occasionally land in repo root
/chart-render.png
/lod-frame.png
serve-explorer.scratch.js
start-local.sh
bing_austin.md

